        FIXHEX.EXE inputfilename.HEX outputfilename.HEX loadaddress data

        Fixhex allows you to replace data at "loadaddress" with the data
        specified in "data". The file must be an Intel hex file. You have
        to know the load address for your data.
        eg. fixbin test.hex out.hex 112ac 01ff02fe03fd04fc05fb06fa07ee08
        Opens file test.hex if it exists and out.hex (can't pre-exist) and
        seeks byte number 112ac(hex) in the address range of the records.
        The program HAS to read the entire file to find any specifed address,
        and then replaces what is there with the data, 
        "01ff02fe03fd04fc05fb06fa07ee08". It displays the replaced data
        as well as the replacing data.
        The syntax must be specified exactly as above, where the load-
        address is in ascii-hex and separates the filenames and the data
        with a single space between each. The data is also ascii-hex and
        may not have a space separating bytes.
